WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.193
Jimmy was a pauper.

2
00:00:02.194 --> 00:00:04.298
He did not have much money.

3
00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:06.233
He did not have much to eat.

4
00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:09.871
He did not have much of anything.

5
00:00:09.872 --> 00:00:12.922
Jimmy spent many days looking for work.

6
00:00:12.923 --> 00:00:15.504
One day he met a farmer.

7
00:00:15.505 --> 00:00:18.589
"Can I work for you?" Jimmy asked him.

8
00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.545
"Yes, but you must work hard," the farmer said.

9
00:00:22.546 --> 00:00:27.333
"I promise, sir," replied Jimmy.

10
00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.447
Jimmy kept his promise.

11
00:00:29.448 --> 00:00:32.321
Every day Jimmy worked hard at the farm.

12
00:00:32.322 --> 00:00:35.219
The farmer and his family liked Jimmy.

13
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.801
His daughter always brought him something to drink.

14
00:00:39.802 --> 00:00:42.430
Jimmy loved to read and study.

15
00:00:42.431 --> 00:00:47.018
He promised himself that one day, he would no longer be a pauper.

16
00:00:47.019 --> 00:00:50.736
"I am going to make my life better," he vowed.

17
00:00:50.737 --> 00:00:56.996
"One day I am going to become an important person."

18
00:00:56.997 --> 00:01:00.680
Every free moment he had, Jimmy read and studied.

19
00:01:00.681 --> 00:01:05.488
"What are you reading, Jimmy?" asked the farmer's daughter one day.

20
00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:10.016
"It's a book about Napoleon," answered Jimmy.

21
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:14.054
Every day the farmer's daughter came to talk with Jimmy.

22
00:01:14.055 --> 00:01:18.509
They talked about books, nature, travel, and their dreams.

23
00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.962
They began to like each other.

24
00:01:20.963 --> 00:01:25.271
The farmer did not know what was going on.

25
00:01:25.272 --> 00:01:28.703
When he saw them together, everything changed.

26
00:01:28.704 --> 00:01:32.616
"What is going on!" the farmer shouted.

27
00:01:32.617 --> 00:01:42.201
"Please, sir, I . . . " Jimmy tried to explain, but the farmer refused to listen.

28
00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:46.637
"My daughter will not marry a pauper!" the farmer shouted.

29
00:01:46.638 --> 00:01:49.591
Then the farmer ordered Jimmy to leave.

30
00:01:49.592 --> 00:01:52.191
"Get out! How dare you!

31
00:01:52.192 --> 00:01:56.069
You are not welcome here anymore!" he shouted.

32
00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:59.802
Poor Jimmy could not say another word to the farmer.

33
00:01:59.803 --> 00:02:04.532
He turned around and left without looking back.

34
00:02:04.533 --> 00:02:09.806
One day, 35 years later, the farmer was cleaning out the stable.

35
00:02:09.807 --> 00:02:14.423
He found an old bag and some books.

36
00:02:14.424 --> 00:02:16.953
The books used to belong to Jimmy.

37
00:02:16.954 --> 00:02:19.519
The farmer opened one of the books.

38
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.770
He was very surprised.

39
00:02:21.771 --> 00:02:24.700
There was a name written inside the book.

40
00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:31.227
It read: James Abram Garfield.

41
00:02:31.228 --> 00:02:35.073
James Abram Garfield was the name of the president.

42
00:02:35.074 --> 00:02:37.801
Jimmy was a nickname for James.

43
00:02:37.802 --> 00:02:40.408
The farmer could not believe it!

44
00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:46.512
Jimmy the pauper was James Garfield─the president!

45
00:02:46.513 --> 00:02:49.995
That day the farmer learned an important lesson:

46
00:02:49.996 --> 00:02:52.560
Never judge a book by its cover.

47
00:02:52.561 --> 00:02:57.429
You should not judge people by the way they look.

48
00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:00.071
Jimmy kept his promise to himself.

49
00:03:00.072 --> 00:03:03.560
After leaving the farm, he studied and worked hard.

50
00:03:03.561 --> 00:03:07.047
He did indeed become an important person.

51
00:03:07.048 --> 00:03:15.752
He went from a life as a pauper to become the twentieth president of the United States.

